## Adaptation boundary

The copied parser and parsed DTOs are intentionally kept independent of MSP
runtime, WorkspaceFS, FFI, Swift, and vendor crates. The crate exposes parsing
and syntax metadata; it does not execute commands or promise execution support
for pipelines, redirections, lists, compound commands, functions, arithmetic,
here documents, or process substitution. Consumers must inspect the returned
AST and choose an explicitly supported execution subset. Forms outside that
subset are represented for syntax inspection or rejected by the single-command
facades with `UnsupportedExecutionForm`.

ReadOS-owned packaging metadata, this notice, and the focused boundary tests
are additions in this workspace. Future source updates must update this map and
retain the upstream license/provenance record.
